 "last_rtl_message": {
  "stage": "constraints",
  "visit": 4,
  "text": "The exceptions gate is still failing, and I couldn't fix it from `design.xdc`. I'm stopping here rather than replying DONE.\n\n- **Cause:** the row it flags is not in my XDC. The flow writes it into `known_post.xdc`. It is `set_max_delay -datapath_only` from `clk_25mhz` to `gt_refclk_p` at 6.4 ns. The XPM macros already constrain every path between those two clocks, so Vivado reports the flow's line as totally overridden. The report names XPM's own false path on the synchroniser inputs (FP 9) and the XPM max-delays on the FIFO Gray pointers (DPO 14, 16, 20).\n- **What I tried:** I added my own `set_clock_groups -asynchronous` between `sys_clk_pin` and `gt_refclk`. I rebuilt through synthesis, and the same row was still ignored, so I reverted it. `design.xdc` is back to the original pins, output delays and the `usr_cclk` false path.\n- **What would clear it:**\n  - The flow's note says to \"state clock_relations\" in `architecture.yaml`. That file is frozen and I don't know the format for that key, so I did not guess at it.\n  - If that key can't be set, the flow generator would have to stop emitting this line for crossings that go through `xpm_fifo_async`, which already carries its own bounds.\n- **Not run:** I did not run `check` with names `[\"all\"]`.\n- **Possible side issue:** `check_constraints` reports FDA-CON-7 on the `clk_25mhz` port name. I did not check whether it also fired before my change."
 },
